   "html_text": "In this section, we will discuss causal models that incorporate probability in some way. Probability may be used to represent our uncertainty about the value of unobserved variables in a particular case, or the distribution of variable values in a population. Often we are interested in when some feature of the causal structure of a system can be identified from the probability distribution over values of variables, perhaps in conjunction with background assumptions and other observations. For ex",
